        {
          kind: "numberedSteps",
          steps: [
            { heading: "Round one. Five minutes, the only answer allowed is no", text: "Offer each other things. Every answer is no. Both of you find out that a no can arrive and nothing breaks." },
            { heading: "Round two. Five minutes, the only answer allowed is yes", text: "Offer again. Every answer is yes." },
            { heading: "Nothing is ever followed through", text: "Not in either round. No tea gets made, no feet get massaged, nobody goes out. The whole thing is noticing what happens in your body as the offer arrives." },
          ],
        },
        {
          kind: "notice",
          lines: [
            { text: "Why offers and not requests", emphasis: "bold" },
            { text: "Saying no to \u201ccan you pass me that\u201d is easy. Saying no to \u201cwould you like me to massage your feet\u201d is not." },
            { text: "You are declining care, which is the one most people genuinely cannot do. Somebody who cannot receive cannot turn down a kindness either, and that is the same muscle.", emphasis: "accent" },
